WEBVTT

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:02.220
Would the same businesses qualify

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:06.310
if a lender considered only
shorter payoff horizons?

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:09.930
In the campaign console,
you can change the policy

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:12.050
and keep the merchants the same.

00:00:12.632 --> 00:00:18.002
For a new population, choose
750 to 25,000 merchants.

00:00:18.612 --> 00:00:21.592
57 settings shape the industry mix,

00:00:21.702 --> 00:00:25.882
daily sales, cash buffers,
financing requests

00:00:25.882 --> 00:00:28.872
and how sales respond to recession stress.

00:00:29.375 --> 00:00:32.095
10 more controls govern lending policy.

00:00:32.395 --> 00:00:37.115
Set the smallest counteroffer,
choose eligible payoff horizons,

00:00:37.305 --> 00:00:40.465
or specify which risks
need an underwriter.

00:00:40.975 --> 00:00:44.445
You can also limit how much
total repayment may increase.

00:00:44.955 --> 00:00:50.265
The parameter guide covers 180
entries, including fixed settings.

00:00:50.705 --> 00:00:53.385
Look up processor tenure minimum.

00:00:53.755 --> 00:00:55.875
It gives the allowed range in months

00:00:55.875 --> 00:00:59.455
and explains how tenure
depends on business age.

00:00:59.945 --> 00:01:02.705
I cap business age at 24 months,

00:01:02.705 --> 00:01:06.535
then require 36 months
with a payment processor.

00:01:07.165 --> 00:01:09.505
Both numbers are allowed individually.

00:01:09.855 --> 00:01:15.015
Together, they require a business to have
processed sales before it existed.

00:01:15.565 --> 00:01:17.715
The console flags the conflict.

00:01:18.258 --> 00:01:20.908
I lower the processor
minimum to 12 months.

00:01:20.908 --> 00:01:24.338
The ranges overlap and
the conflict clears.

00:01:24.668 --> 00:01:26.688
Policy settings have checks too.

00:01:27.198 --> 00:01:32.068
A 3% automatic cost increase
exceeds a 2% review limit.

00:01:32.898 --> 00:01:35.398
The run still checks the generated data.

00:01:35.998 --> 00:01:40.118
To test shorter offers,
reuse a saved population

00:01:40.118 --> 00:01:41.468
and choose Challenger.

00:01:41.868 --> 00:01:46.298
Keep 30 and 60 days eligible. Turn off 90.

00:01:46.778 --> 00:01:50.748
Now you can compare who
qualifies and who needs review

00:01:50.988 --> 00:01:54.000
using the same merchants
and sales histories.

